                                "sense_id": "d8aa8e00-1449-3b40-ae3e-c65ee3a1507e",
                                "text": "Institutionalism is brought about, in part, by a sense of learned helplessness, a belief that one has no control over one's environment."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "47692fae-3b7b-4ff0-aa70-4b275f2c45c3",
                                "sense_id": "d8aa8e00-1449-3b40-ae3e-c65ee3a1507e",
                                "text": "Therefore, in addition to noting the similarities between the \"new Nietzsche\" and nonabsolutist institutionalism, we want to show briefly what, specifically, a reading of Nietzsche adds to the institutionalist treatment of values."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
